The aim of this campaign is to increase the political participation of disability communities while also engaging candidates and the media on disability issues. ATVFL invites all stakeholders and advocates in the state to collaborate on effective, nonpartisan efforts to:

Address the concerns of people with disabilities;
Eliminate barriers to voting;
Educate people with disabilities about issues and candidates;
Promote turnout of voters with disabilities; and
Engage candidates and the media on disability issues.

**Super PACs are destroying what’s left of American democracy.**

For over a decade, these billionaire-funded mega-PACs have served as legal loopholes, allowing corporations and the ultra-wealthy to pump unlimited, often anonymous money into our elections. They buy influence. They drown out real voters. And they do it all while claiming to be “independent.”

The Abolish Super PACs Act (H.R.2352) is the strongest legislation in Congress to end this abuse once and for all. It:

-   Caps donations to Super PACs at $5,000 per person, per year;
-   Closes the “coordination” loophole that lets candidates and PACs act like one team;
-   Restores electoral integrity by shifting power from billionaires back to the people.

This bill has overwhelming public support. A NYT/CBS poll found that  **78% of Americans across party lines**  support limiting Super PAC money. But Congress still refuses to act.  **Why? Because many of them benefit from the corruption.**

**That ends now.**

**Use this form to send a direct message to your Senators and Representatives demanding they:**

-   Cosponsor H.R.2352;
-   Speak out publicly in favor of abolishing Super PACs;
-   Push for hearings and a vote—no more stalling.

This is a test of who works for us—and who works for their donors. Let’s make the answer clear.
